Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. FARMHOUSE - TUESDAY - MORNING

An old bicycle stands in the yard, chain loose. Elias admits he left without a note to place the farm van at the livestock market under its old agricultural account.

ZOE
Next time, leave a note.

ELIAS
Yes.

On a newspaper photograph, everyone watches a politician except a man watching the exit.

ELIAS
Don't look at the threat. Look at what changes around it.

They agree on a conversational signal: THE FLOWERS ARE WRONG.

INT./EXT. MARKET TOWN - DAY

At the chemist Elias stays six metres away while Zoe chooses her own personal supplies. Schoolgirls recommend a cheaper shampoo. For a moment she has an ordinary choice. They buy food, yellow-striped socks and a plain blue notebook.

At a dark shop window, Zoe studies the reflected flower stall. A man buys lilies but watches the fish van's reflected square. A woman reads at the cafe, repaired scuff on her left heel. A bus blocks their view; she closes her book. A black saloon replaces the bus at the kerb.

ZOE
The flowers are wrong.

Elias keeps walking. She gives the sequence without looking back. He tests alternatives; she distinguishes what she saw from what she thinks it means.

ELIAS
Possibly the man from the cottage.

ZOE
You didn't see him.

ELIAS
You described him.

They finish the list. In another reflection Zoe sees the woman again, different bag, same repaired heel.

ZOE
Same book. Same shoes.

INT./EXT. CAR PARK/ROADS/LIVESTOCK MARKET - LATER

They leave the lift a floor early and walk up the ramp. At a faulty barrier the following car waits without impatience. Vehicles change during their circuit; Elias avoids the farmhouse road.

Voss receives sightings from Reyes and Vale, not a new tracker.

VALE (EARPIECE)
Detection confirmed. She signalled; he reacted.

At a reservoir dead end no tail enters. Back at the junction, the red van returns.

ELIAS
They're patient. We stop using the car they know.

At the livestock market they leave the estate under the auction building. In the cafe Zoe sees Vale questioning staff. A cattle lorry blocks the view as workers open a service gate.

ZOE
She watches the public exits. Nobody covers that one.

They collect the pre-positioned farm van with a key and an ordinary explanation. Shopping goes into crates; Zoe keeps her backpack. They leave with other white vans through the service gate.

EXT. LAY-BY - LATER

No repeated vehicle after further checks. Zoe holds the unwanted jar of honey.

ZOE
They may know it was me. You could tell me to stop.

ELIAS
Not seeing them wouldn't stop them seeing you. I trust what you notice.

INT. FARMHOUSE - NIGHT

They unpack. Yellow socks beside her notebook. Elias tastes the honey with exaggerated seriousness.

ELIAS
Average.

Zoe laughs, briefly. Then writes: TRUST IS ALSO A PATTERN.
